OL,3,GNEWSAIOPC to probe if police could have
OL,4,Astopped killing
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe police watchdog is investigating
OL,7,Fwhether officers missed an opportunity
OL,8,Fto prevent a psychotic stranger
OL,9,Fstabbing a disabled woman to death in
OL,10,Fthe victim's home.
OL,12,FPatricia Hewitt, 42, had been allowed
OL,13,Fto walk away by Durham Police officers
OL,14,Fminutes before she killed Angela Lloyd,
OL,15,F56, in Newton Aycliffe in August 2025.
OL,17,FAfter initially being unable to
OL,18,Finvestigate as their remit was not met,
OL,19,Fthe Independent Office for Police
OL,20,FConduct (IOPC) said a probe had been
OL,21,Flaunched after receiving a complaint,
OL,22,Fbelieved to be from Lloyd's family.
OL,23,APub: 08-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
